  "notes": "Zone and stops from gtfs-flex.zip (Spare GTFS-Flex Editor export of 2026-10-13), sent by Ride Connection (operator) to Atlas Outreach on 2026-10-13. The zone is the feed's one location, 'Mountainside Boundary' (locations.geojson, with its 4 holes), used exactly as given; it is named from the feed's route description. The 14 stops are the feed's one location group (stops.txt): Washington Square Transit Center, schools, Cooper Mountain Nature Park and 7 stops east of Murray Blvd, all outside the zone; the feed allows trips between the zone and these stops. Calendar runs 2026-09-01 to 2030-01-05, weekdays. The feed's booking window is 6 a.m. to 9:45 p.m.; the hours shown are the rider page's (6:30 a.m. first pickup, 9:30 p.m. last drop-off). Open to everyone and free (catchthespot.org: 'It's for everyone'); funded by a STIF grant through Washington County. Pickup is where the rider is (page), but no curb or door rule is stated, so no pickup method is set. Not attached to TriMet: SPOT is run by Washington County and Ride Connection."
}
